  "prompt": "Use case: scientific-educational. Asset type: individual vocabulary images for a Japanese children's shiritori dictionary.\nEDIT TARGET: attached 2048x2048 equal 4 by 4 white grid template. Paint exactly sixteen independent illustrations into its cells, in row-major order, left to right then top to bottom. Preserve the exact canvas size, all cell dimensions, ALL FIVE horizontal and FIVE vertical continuous pure MAGENTA #ff00ff lines INCLUDING the outer frame, their positions, straightness and thickness. Do not erase, cover, move or redraw dividers. Magenta is reserved only for the grid. No extra panels, no captions, labels, letters, numerals, logos or watermarks.\nStyle: clear gentle natural-history picture-book illustration with accurate species anatomy and distinguishing colors. Each complete subject and its shadow stays inside its own cell; use the cell generously, no mandatory large margins. Light neutral background. Never substitute another species or invent variety-specific coloration. Crop must not amputate the subject. For rice cultivars use botanically plausible ordinary green/gold rice panicles and pale grains, with a small plain bowl of cooked white rice only for table-rice cultivars. Sake-rice shows panicle and uncooked rice, without alcohol bottles. Forage-rice shows lush rice stems/leaves, without a cooked-rice bowl. Cultivar illustrations are illustrative examples, never diagnostic identification photographs.\nSixteen subjects in exact order:\n1. シロマダラ (Lycodon orientalis): 白っぽい体に黒褐色の帯模様がある日本のヘビの仲間の爬虫類。主に夜に動く。\n2. ジムグリ (Euprepiophis conspicillata): 日本にすむヘビの仲間の爬虫類。土や落ち葉の下にも潜り小さな哺乳類などを食べる。\n3. ヒバカリ (Hebius vibakari): 首の後ろに白い模様がある小さなヘビの仲間の爬虫類。水辺などで見られる。\n4. タカチホヘビ (Achalinus spinalis): つやのある体と小さな頭を持つヘビの仲間の爬虫類。土や落ち葉の下でミミズなどを食べる。\n5. アカマタ (Lycodon semicarinatus): 赤茶色の地に黒っぽい帯があるヘビの仲間の爬虫類。沖縄諸島や奄美諸島などにすむ。\n6. ヒメハブ (Ovophis okinavensis): 短く太めの体を持つ毒のあるヘビの仲間の爬虫類。南西諸島の一部にすむ。\n7. サキシマハブ (Protobothrops elegans): 八重山諸島にすむ毒のあるヘビの仲間の爬虫類。体に暗い色の模様が並ぶ。\n8. トカラハブ (Protobothrops tokarensis): トカラ列島の一部にすむ毒のあるヘビの仲間の爬虫類。\n9. ハイ (Sinomicrurus boettgeri): 沖縄諸島の一部にすむコブラの仲間の爬虫類。小さな体を持つ毒ヘビ。\n10. ヒャン (Sinomicrurus japonicus): 奄美大島などにすむコブラの仲間の爬虫類。細い体に帯模様がある毒ヘビ。\n11. エラブウミヘビ (Laticauda semifasciata): 平たい尾と帯模様を持つ毒のある爬虫類。海で魚を食べ陸にも上がる。\n12. アオマダラウミヘビ (Laticauda laticaudata): 青みのある体に黒い帯模様を持つ毒のある爬虫類。海と陸を行き来する。\n13. クロガシラウミヘビ (Hydrophis melanocephalus): 頭が黒っぽく体に帯模様がある毒のあるヘビの仲間の爬虫類。海で暮らす。\n14. イイジマウミヘビ (Emydocephalus ijimae): 魚の卵を主に食べるウミヘビの仲間の爬虫類。平たい尾で泳ぐ。\n15. セグロウミヘビ (Hydrophis platurus): 黒っぽい背中と黄色いおなかを持つ毒のあるヘビの仲間の爬虫類。海面近くを泳ぐ。\n16. トゲウミヘビ (Hydrophis ornatus): 海で暮らす毒のあるヘビの仲間の爬虫類。平たい尾を持ち魚などを食べる。\nAll snakes have a single anatomically continuous body, one head and one tail, no legs, no extra heads. Use natural adult/wild-type colors and morphology for the exact scientific species. No attacking people, bites, wounds or gore. Venomous and nonvenomous species are depicted observationally.\nSpecies-specific visual checks from Japanese herpetology references:\nCell 9 Hai (Sinomicrurus boettgeri): small slender coral snake, orange to reddish-brown ground color, FIVE black LENGTHWISE stripes; do not replace with a generic ringed American coral snake. Cell 10 Hyan (Sinomicrurus japonicus), representative Amami adult: orange ground, spaced black rings around the body combined with a black mid-dorsal LENGTHWISE stripe; black snout/head. These are separate Japanese species, not Naja cobras, so do NOT draw a spread hood.\nCell 6 Ovophis okinavensis: stout short gray-brown pitviper with dark blotches; no rattles. Cells 11-16 sea snakes have a laterally flattened paddle tail, not a fish fin or legs. Cell 15 Hydrophis platurus: sharply black upper body and bright yellow lower body; no blue bands on its trunk. Cell 13 Hydrophis melanocephalus: dark head, yellowish body with dark crossbands. Cell 14 Emydocephalus ijimae: blunt small head, black and pale banding, paddle tail. Cell 1 Lycodon orientalis: pale-gray/white ground with dark transverse blotches; no red rings. All sixteen are separate complete snakes, no intertwined bodies from neighboring panels.\n\nEDIT OF GENERATED SHEET: first reference is the generated sheet to repair; the template is a geometry reference. Change ONLY cell 2 (top row, second column), Jimuguri Euprepiophis conspicillata, into a slender adult Japanese forest ratsnake: smooth copper/rusty reddish-brown back with only tiny sparse dark dots, small oval head merging into the neck, rounded pupils. NO large diamond/saddle blotches, NO broad viper-like head, NO rattles. Keep a few leaf-litter pieces. Preserve every other cell, including the stripe/ring difference of Hai and Hyan. Keep all magenta lines, exact 4x4 cell placement and overall canvas; no labels or extra panels.",
